// Stryker config for PR runs only (mutation.yml passes it with --config-file; the nightly
// full sweep does not, because a "since" object here turns incremental mode on).
//
// ignore-changes-in drops test-side paths from the --since diff. Stryker 5.0.0's MTP runner
// registers every test with an empty file path (MtpTestDescription), and SinceMutantFilter
// treats an empty path as "this test changed" whenever any test .cs file is in the diff, so a
// PR that touched one test re-ran every covered mutant of the project: a full sweep of
// Equiv.Core (1251 mutants, 92 min on M3-013). A changed non-.cs file under the test project
// (a *.verified.txt snapshot, the .csproj) re-ran every mutant outright. With test paths
// ignored, a PR is held to the mutants in the src files it changed, tested against the full
// new test suite (QUALITY-GATES.md, Mutation row); the nightly sweep catches a test edit that
// lets a mutant in an unchanged file survive.
{
  "stryker-config": {
    "since": {
      "ignore-changes-in": ["**/tests/**"]
    }
  }
}
